    "source": "United Energy 2026-27 Pricing (structure) + AER-published TSS 2026-31 SCS Indicative Prices (rates) + United Energy 2026-27 SCS pricing model filed with the AER (7 May 2026; URSTOU rates)",
    "source_url": "https://www.aer.gov.au/system/files/2026-05/United%20Energy%20%E2%80%93%202026%E2%80%9327%20%E2%80%93%20Pricing%20%E2%80%93%207%20May%202026.pdf",
    "effective_from": "2026-07-01",
    "notes": "Excluding GST. Residential ToU URSTOU: peak 4pm-9pm, saver 11am-4pm, off-peak 9pm-11am, all days, rates from the United Energy 2026-27 SCS pricing model filed with the AER (7 May 2026; knowledge/documents/united-energy/2026-11-10-scs-pricing-model-2026-27). Small business ToU peak is 9am-9pm workdays. Residential/export CER tariffs and all demand-charge tariffs (LVMKW1R/UMBD/UMBO/large/HV) are NOT seeded -- same reasoning as citipower.json/powercor.json (single-window demand schema can't represent United Energy's two-season summer/non-summer demand charge without an unmade modeling decision). Source PDF gives tariff codes/structure but not $ rates -- those live in the United Energy 2026-27 SCS pricing model filed with the AER (7 May 2026), which gives URSTOU rates; rates for the other tariffs here are still sourced from AER's regulator-hosted TSS.01 indicative-prices spreadsheet (2026-31 Tariff Structure Statement, Jan2025 proposal), cross-checked against the structural PDF's tariff codes (exact match: LVS1R, LVDed, URSTOU, LVM1R, LVTOU). 'Indicative' prices, not a final DNSP-published price list -- flagged as a slightly different provenance tier than other seeded DNSPs.",
    "last_verified": "2026-08-03"
  },
